e next-level performance.\\n+\\n+Decision Rationale\\n+- Bar not met this cycle: Insufficient sustained evidence of next-level scope and predictability due to the timing and duration of absence within the review window.\\n+- Calibration: Compared to peers promoted this cycle, successful candidates demonstrated uninterrupted ownership of multi-month initiatives, predictable on-call participation, and consistent cross-team leadership signals.\\n+\\n+Development Plan and Next Steps\\n+- Re-establish Baseline: Focus on a full cycle of uninterrupted ownership for a clearly defined roadmap project (e.g., Crawler Dedup Index v2 rollout) with explicit milestones and success criteria.\\n+- Predictability Signals: Commit to a documented availability plan and on-call rotation for the cycle; complete incident follow-ups within SLA to demonstrate reliability.\\n+- Scope Expansion: Lead a cross-team effort (coordination with Data Platform and Infra) including design, dependency management, and post-rollout metrics.\\n+- Evidence Capture: Track progress via OKRs, milestone burndown, incident postmortems, and review throughput to ensure objective artifacts for the next promotion review.\\n+\\n+Promotion Reconsideration Criteria\\n+We will be ready to reconsider promotion once there is:\\n+- One full review cycle of sustained delivery at the next-level scope, including demonstrated predictability in availability and commitments.\\n+- Clear artifacts showing end-to-end ownership and cross-team coordination.\\n+- Positive calibration against peers based on impact, reliability, and leadership behaviors.\\n+\\n+Addendum: Data Sources on File\\n+- Jira epics and milestone burndown for the crawler reliability work (current and prior cycles)\\n+- On-call schedules and incident follow-up records\\n+- Code review participation and merge metrics\\n+- Project status updates and design review notes', _diff_cache=None), AgentFinishAction(final_thought='I read the task file at /instruction/task.m